<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2010/07/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>MegaForm.Oqtane</id>
    <version>$version$</version>
    <authors>MegaForm Team</authors>
    <owners>MegaForm</owners>
    <title>MegaForm - Dynamic Form Builder</title>
    <description>Dynamic Form Builder for Oqtane — drag-and-drop form designer with templates, multi-step forms, conditional logic, payment widgets, rules engine, and submissions management.</description>
    <copyright>MegaForm Team</copyright>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/nicknguyen-oqtane/MegaForm</projectUrl>
    <icon>icon.png</icon>
    <tags>oqtane module form builder survey payment</tags>
    <releaseNotes>v2.0.3 (20260725) — 🖼️ TEMPLATE PREVIEWS AND THUMBNAILS NOW LOOK LIKE THE REAL FORM. Gallery cards and the preview dialog render the template's real MegaForm field markup so the template's own styling applies; the preview is a full self-contained snapshot (hero, stepper, sections, fields) instead of a live renderer that had hidden the hero pane; cross-platform hero images are rewritten to the current platform so they stop 404-ing. {{field:ROWKEY}} tokens that reference a Row container now render the row's child fields (some forms previously showed empty "Field placeholder" boxes), the {{form:submit}} token no longer paints a second button inside the template's own submit button, and the preview iframe height no longer runs away on resize. AssetVersion 20260725-B410.

v2.0.2 (20260725) — 🖼️ TEMPLATE PREVIEWS AND THUMBNAILS NOW LOOK LIKE THE REAL FORM. Gallery cards and the preview dialog render the template's real MegaForm field markup (.mf-input, .mf-option-group/chips/cards, .mf-select …) so a template's own styling applies. The preview shows a full self-contained snapshot (hero, stepper, sections, fields) instead of a live renderer that had hidden the hero pane. Cross-platform hero images are rewritten to the current platform so they stop 404-ing. This build also fixes two field-level rendering bugs: {{field:ROWKEY}} tokens that reference a Row container now render the row's child fields (some forms previously showed empty "Field placeholder" boxes), and the {{form:submit}} token no longer paints a second differently-coloured button inside the template's own submit button. AssetVersion 20260725-B409.

v2.0.1 (20260725) — 🖼️ TEMPLATE PREVIEWS AND THUMBNAILS NOW LOOK LIKE THE REAL FORM. Gallery cards and the preview dialog render the template's real MegaForm field markup (.mf-input, .mf-option-group/chips/cards, .mf-select …), so a template's own styling applies and the card looks like the form instead of generic grey boxes. The preview dialog shows a full, self-contained snapshot of the template — hero, stepper, sections and fields at natural size — instead of a live renderer instance that inherited the dashboard's guards (which had hidden the hero pane). Cross-platform hero images are fixed: a template authored for DNN referenced /DesktopModules/… image paths that 404 on Oqtane (and vice-versa), leaving an empty hero and mis-read overlay colours; module image URLs are now rewritten to the current platform at render time. Thumbnails are fitted to their card at runtime (they were painted at a hard-coded scale, cropped into the corner), each card shows the template's name + category + field count, and stray {{script:*}} tokens no longer leak into the preview.

v2.0.0 (20260724) — 🚀 A FRESH INSTALL NOW OPENS A FULL TEMPLATE SHELF, AND THE ONLINE GALLERY IS BROWSABLE ON TRIAL. The Template Gallery ships with 31 free quick-start starters (contact, booking, application, education, nonprofit, and a floating-label set) plus 4 premium designs on display — 35 templates to build from immediately, offline, on a brand-new or trial install. Previously a trial install saw only premium cards, every one of them locked. The online gallery is now a real shop window: a trial install can browse and preview every premium design (thumbnails, full preview, field counts) and is only refused the download — installing still needs a paid license, enforced server-side. Every card now carries the template's NAME and a category/field-count line instead of being an unlabelled picture, and the live thumbnail is fitted to the card at runtime (it used to render at a hard-coded scale, leaving the design in the top-left corner with bare background around it). Licensing on Oqtane is driven entirely by the Oqtane Marketplace: no license file ships in this package, so an install runs in trial until a Marketplace key is activated. Package is ~15 MB lighter: template artwork lives in the gallery repo instead of the module.

v1.7.114 (20260724) — A FRESH INSTALL NOW OPENS A FULL TEMPLATE SHELF. The Template Gallery ships with 31 free quick-start starters (contact, booking, application, education, nonprofit, and a floating-label set) plus 4 premium designs on display — so a brand-new or trial install has 35 templates to build from immediately, offline. Previously a trial install saw only premium cards, every one of them locked. Fixes the root cause: "premium" was inferred from the mere presence of a custom-HTML layout wrapper, which the free starters also carry; templates now declare it, and template SHAPE (custom shell — must survive Create) is tracked separately from LICENSING (locked on trial). Licensing on Oqtane is driven entirely by the Oqtane Marketplace: no license file ships in this package, so an install runs in trial until a Marketplace key is activated, and the online gallery (every remaining premium design + all hero artwork, served over a CDN and sha256-pinned) unlocks with it. Package is ~15 MB lighter: template artwork now lives in the gallery repo instead of the module.

v1.7.107 (20260717) — 🎨 PREMIUM TEMPLATE THEME INHERITANCE. All 14 non-locked premium form templates (DONEE set) now follow the host page theme when "Color source = From page" is enabled — card surface, title/label/input text, input backgrounds, borders, buttons and step indicators all borrow the Bootstrap/Bootswatch host palette together, so a form on a dark or coloured Oqtane theme is coherent and readable instead of a white card with invisible text. Each template's palette layer chains through a page channel then a preset channel then its authored colour, so the DEFAULT look is byte-for-byte identical (verified: 26/26 screenshots 0 pixel change). Manifest v2 (settings.themeCompatibility.policy) drives it: 'tokenized'/'hybrid' opt in; 3 brand templates (Festa Italiana, Americana Journey, Bulgaria Discovery) are 'locked' and keep their authored identity; immutable brand assets (Facebook/GitHub buttons, photo heroes, gradient identity, status colours) never retheme. Date/multiselect popovers (.mf-cal/.mf-ms/.mf-mccb) now couple their text/border/hover to the form colours so they are legible on dark hosts. Template JSON structure normalised (deduped customCss/customHtml, dropped dual-case keys). AssetVersion 20260717-B405. \n\nv1.7.105 (20260713) — 📎 FILE UPLOAD PROVEN E2E + 📥 MY INBOX FIXED + 🖨️ PER-SUBMISSION PRINT + 🤖 AI DATA-SOURCE PICKER. (1) File upload on rendered Oqtane pages now actually uploads (client fires POST Upload/File with metadata written into the submission; server returns files in GET Submissions/{id}; duplicate MF_Files rows deduped; grid shows a download link instead of raw JSON). (2) My Inbox displays the truth: the Assigned-to-Me badge counts name-matched ad-hoc tasks, claimed tasks read "In Review" instead of "Pending", task ages are timezone-correct (UTC parsing), submitter names resolve (the submitters map was dropped by the client normalizer), Send-to-Inbox resolves the target user (unknown user → clear 400) and the toast says where the task landed. (3) NEW GET Submissions/{id}/Print on all four platforms — the form's Print layout merged with the submitted values (filled fields, ticked choices, line-item rows, INVOICED/REJECTED stamp) behind the same row-level view gate as the submission itself; Print buttons in the inbox detail and the submissions sheet. (4) The AI form creator's Database tab can now browse allow-listed Settings connections (MegaForm:ExternalTables:AllowedConnections) besides the current database, and instructs the AI to stamp optionsConnectionKey on SQL-backed fields. (5) ATBE capability card + AI designer strings de-hardcoded to English-default i18n (atbe.* keys, Vietnamese via vi-VN.json). AssetVersion 20260713-B397. Everything from 1.7.104 (payments proven with a real card) carries forward.</releaseNotes>
    <summary>Dynamic form builder module for Oqtane CMS</summary>

    <packageTypes>
      <!-- "Dependency" is the standard NuGet library type — confirmed working by CISS.SideMenu reference -->
      <packageType name="Dependency" />
      <!-- Oqtane.Framework: minimum compatible framework version — read by InstallationManager XPath -->
      <packageType name="Oqtane.Framework" version="6.1.2" />
    </packageTypes>

    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework="net9.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         COMPLETENESS (verified in v1.7.27): this package is COMPLETE for a clean Oqtane install —
         · DLLs: all MegaForm assemblies (Client/Server/Shared/Core/Sdk) + non-host deps
           (Newtonsoft.Json, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Razor.Language, Microsoft.CodeAnalysis[.CSharp]),
           for BOTH net9.0 and net10.0 (entries below).
         · KBs / SQL scripts: the wwwroot wildcard ships all KB content under
           wwwroot\Modules\MegaForm\Resources\ (34 TemplateGuide .md + PromptRecipes) + all js/css/
           fonts/img. The MF_* table "SQL scripts" are the EF migrations COMPILED INTO the Server DLL
           (Migrations\*.cs + EntityBuilders) — not standalone files — so they ship inside lib\*.
         ⭐ For a COMPLETE build, run the full `pack.cmd` (it npm-builds the 7 JS bundles + Vite-syncs
            them into MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\wwwroot BEFORE packing). A lean re-pack only refreshes
            what's already in that wwwroot — stale/missing bundles there → an incomplete package.
         ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- net9.0 builds -->

    <!-- Client Blazor WASM DLL — tên chứa "Oqtane" → được load bởi IsOqtaneAssembly() -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- Server DLL — tên chứa "Oqtane" → được load -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- Shared DLL — tên chứa "Oqtane" → được load -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- Core DLL — tên KHÔNG chứa "Oqtane" → KHÔNG được load vào AppDomain -->
    <!-- Nhưng vẫn cần trong bin/ vì Client/Server DLL có reference đến nó -->
    <!-- .NET runtime sẽ tự resolve khi cần (dependency resolution) -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Core.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- Third-party dependencies not provided by Oqtane host -->
    <!-- Newtonsoft.Json is used by MegaForm.Core; Oqtane 6 does NOT ship it -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Newtonsoft.Json.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <!-- [pkg-fix 20260625] MegaForm runtime deps the Oqtane host does NOT provide. Without these a
         CLEAN-host install crashes at startup (ReflectionTypeLoadException during Oqtane's assembly
         scan): MegaForm.Sdk → Microsoft.AspNetCore.Razor.Language → Roslyn (CodeAnalysis). The
         :5070 dev site only worked because it had accumulated them from earlier manual deploys. -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Sdk.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Microsoft.AspNetCore.Razor.Language.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- [CloudStorage v20260723-01] Cloud storage providers (Google Drive / Amazon S3 / Azure
         Blob) for the post-submit file mirror. AWSSDK + Azure.Storage are NOT provided by the
         Oqtane host, so they must ship inside the package. -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\MegaForm.Integrations.CloudStorage.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\AWSSDK.Core.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\AWSSDK.S3.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Azure.Core.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Azure.Storage.Blobs.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Azure.Storage.Common.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- [OqtaneLicensing v20260723] Oqtane Marketplace licensing (LicenseView + offline key
         validation). Names contain "Oqtane" → loaded by IsOqtaneAssembly(); Client/Shared are
         also declared in ModuleInfo.Dependencies (required for Blazor WebAssembly). -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Client.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Server.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net9.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Shared.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net9.0" />

    <!-- net10.0 builds (Oqtane 10.x hosts, e.g. :5070 Oqtane.MSSQL3 + :5000 Oqtane.New10) -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Client.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Oqtane.Shared.Oqtane.pdb" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Core.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Newtonsoft.Json.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Sdk.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Microsoft.AspNetCore.Razor.Language.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\MegaForm.Integrations.CloudStorage.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\AWSSDK.Core.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\AWSSDK.S3.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Azure.Core.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Azure.Storage.Blobs.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Azure.Storage.Common.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <!-- [OqtaneLicensing v20260723] see net9.0 note above -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Client.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Server.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\bin\Release\net10.0\Oqtane.Licensing.Shared.Oqtane.dll" target="lib\net10.0" />

    <!-- FIX 3: wwwroot — path đúng: wwwroot/Modules/MegaForm/** → deploy vào {webroot}/Modules/MegaForm/ -->
    <!-- Oqtane extract: bỏ 1 segment "wwwroot" → còn Modules/MegaForm/... → vào wwwroot/Modules/MegaForm/ -->
    <!-- [LicenseEdition 2026-07-24] EXCLUDE license.lic: on Oqtane, licensing is driven purely by the
         Oqtane Marketplace (OqtaneLicenseBridge). Shipping license.lic="production" would auto-license
         every install and make the Marketplace/trial gate moot. A fresh Oqtane install is therefore
         TRIAL until a Marketplace key is activated (then the bridge flips IsProductionLicensed). -->
    <file src="..\MegaForm.Oqtane.Server\wwwroot\Modules\MegaForm\**\*.*" target="wwwroot\Modules\MegaForm" exclude="**\license.lic;**\img\brochure-youth\brochure-youth-hero.jpg;**\img\bulgaria-discovery\bulgaria-plovdiv.png;**\img\bulgaria-discovery\bulgaria-rose-hero.png;**\img\euro-youth\euro-youth-hero.png;**\img\festa-italiana\festa-italiana-hero.png;**\img\festa-italiana\festa-italiana-texture.png;**\img\floral-youth\floral-youth-hero.jpg;**\img\mock\americana-coast.png;**\img\mock\americana-hero.png;**\img\mock\outback-station-side.png;**\img\realestate-registration\header-illus.png;**\img\teal-brochure\teal-brochure-hero.jpg;**\img\vintage-americana-header.png" />

    <!-- Package metadata -->
    <file src="icon.png" target="" />
    <file src="license.txt" target="" />
    <!-- Note: license.lic is deliberately EXCLUDED from the wwwroot wildcard above (Oqtane =
         Marketplace-licensed, not file-licensed). Do NOT re-add it here. -->
  </files>
</package>
